{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Reuben, you are my firstborn.</b> You were worthy to take a double portion in the birthright, and also the priesthood was worthy to be yours, for the service was performed by the firstborn, and also the kingship, for the kingship belongs to the firstborn, as it is said: ״ואת הממלכה נתן ליהורם כי הוא הבכור״. But you did not merit to have the birthright, and it was given to Joseph, and the priesthood to Levi, and the kingship to Judah. Thus it is written: ״כי עלה משכביך אז חללת יצועיו״ — ״נתנה בכורתו ליוסף״. And what caused this to you? Because you acted impetuously like water — like a jug that is spilled, leaving nothing to you except the counting, for the counting always begins from Reuben. And therefore it says כמים — for water is a moist thing, and some of it remains in the vessel, unlike a dry thing from which nothing remains. And in tractate Shabbat in the chapter במה בהמה, it concludes: כתנאי — 'פחז': Rabbi Elazar says: פזתה חבתה זלתה. Rabbi Yehoshua says: פסעתה על דת, חטאת, זנית. Rabbi Gornishli [Rabban Gamliel] says: פללתה חללת זרחה תפלתך. Rabbi Elazar HaModa'i says: invert and expound it — זעזעת חרתעתה פרחה חטא ממך. Rava says: זכרת עונשו של דבר, חלית עצמך חולי גדול, פרשת מלחטוא." "<b>Like water, do not excel.</b> Like water that is poured from a vessel, from which nothing remains — and not like oil, which remains in the vessel after it is poured."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {0 "The names Rabbi Gornishli and Rabbi Elazar HaModa'i are preserved as they appear; the former likely refers to Rabban Gamliel. The Aramaic punning interpretations (on the letters peh-ḥet-zayin of פחזת) are translated literally with their wordplay intact."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:29.092718572Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}